	)
	(text_box "Non-inverting amplifier, gain = 1 + 100k/10k = 11 (20.8 dB). R10/R11 bias the input to 1.65V (mid-supply) for single-supply operation. C32 (10µF) decouples the bias point at AC so it acts as a solid virtual ground for the signal. C30 AC-couples the Sallen-Key output to remove any DC offset from the filter. Output goes to RP2040 ADC (GP26/ADC0). Full-scale ADC input is 0–3.3V; with 1.65V bias, the signal can swing ±1.65V before clipping. Gain of 11 may need adjustment based on actual signal levels — change R13 to tune. MCP6022 GBW = 10 MHz, well above the ~~3 kHz signal band."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 281.94 149.6822 0)
		(size -45.72 38.1)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
			(color 0 0 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 150 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "710b5680-a123-4106-b731-ab84916652b5")
	)
	(text_box "Sallen-Key topology per Art of Electronics Fig 6.16A. C28 is the FEEDBACK capacitor — connects from the R8/R9 junction to the op-amp output. C29 goes from IN+ to GND. This is NOT two caps to ground — C28's feedback to the output is what creates the complex pole pair and gives -40 dB/decade rolloff (2nd order). With R8=R9 and C28=C29 (equal-component Butterworth), Q = 0.707, no ringing. fc = 1/(2π×R×C) = 1/(2π×22k×2.2nF) = 3,289 Hz. LTspice verified: -3dB at 2,985 Hz, 1200 Hz passes at -0.56 dB, 2200 Hz at -1.75 dB. C0G/NP0 caps required for filter accuracy.\n\nMCP6022-I/SN - prototype\nMCP6022-I/ST - flight"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 99.06 143.3322 0)
		(size -68.58 33.02)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
			(color 0 0 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 150 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7656163a-6249-44ab-b4b6-9c3cfee8a6f4")
	)
	(text_box "435 MHz preselector: 3-pole LC, 10 nH 0402HP (Q~55), centered 435 MHz. Rejects out-of-band signals before the LNA; sets front-end selectivity.\n\nAll capacitors C0G/NP0. Starting values (VNA-tune in bring-up): I/O coupling caps Ccpl = 6 pF, shunt resonator caps Cres = 36 pF, inductors 10 nH 0402HP. NOTE: the four BPF caps (C29-C32) are all still 10 pF from the old 2m design -- in the schematic editor set the two SHUNT (resonator) caps to 36 pF and the two SERIES (I/O coupling) caps to 6 pF.\n\nAll-UHF: FM broadcast (88-108 MHz) is 4x away and trivially rejected -- the old 2m FM/notch problem is GONE. Do NOT try to reject 437 MHz TX leakage here: TX and RX are both ~435-437 (in band). The half-duplex T/R switch provides TX isolation, not this filter. Job now: low insertion loss (protects NF) + reject the LO 2nd harmonic (870 MHz). Sim: rx_circuit.asc (IL ~1.9 dB, FM -49 dB)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 127 67.1322 0)
		(size -96.52 25.4)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
			(color 0 0 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 150 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c840ed36-de8f-4653-a3e6-715e696c5da1")
	)
	(text_box "RX LO = 435 MHz via TRIPLER (replaces the old direct-145.9 LO + 5-pole LPF, now obsolete). Si5351A CLK1 @145 MHz -> 2SC3356 class-C tripler -> collector tank (15 nH || 8.2 pF) -> 435 MHz BPF -> LO amp -> pad to +7 dBm at the ADE-1+ LO port. Clone of the TX tripler front end; sim rx_lo_tripler.asc (x3 -> 435 at ~+12 dBm, then pad down to +7).\n\nThe old 5-pole Butterworth LPF (L12/L13 = 68 nH, C22/C23/C24) is REMOVED: a tripler synthesizes 435 from 145, which an LPF on a 145 LO cannot do. C0G/NP0 on all RF caps. This whole block is GUI rework -- see the LO tripler build spec."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 283.21 33.02 0)
		(size 86.36 22.86)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
			(color 0 0 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 150 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d496d103-e41f-4b4b-954b-bd69f5848f8d")
	)
	(text_box "RX CHAIN -- 435 MHz uplink receiver (all-UHF, half-duplex, zero-IF). A 435 MHz preselector rejects out-of-band signals before the LNA. A PSA4-5043+ MMIC LNA sets the system noise figure and recovers the ADE-1+ passive mixer conversion loss. The ADE-1+ double-balanced diode mixer downconverts 435 to baseband using a 435 MHz LO derived from Si5351A CLK1 (@145) through an x3 tripler, padded to +7 dBm. A 51 ohm resistor terminates the mixer IF port. A 2nd-order Sallen-Key LPF (fc ~3.3 kHz) filters the baseband, then an MCP6022 amplifies (x11) to the RP2040 ADC.\n\nHalf-duplex: RX and TX share one UHF antenna via a T/R switch; the transmitter is off during receive. (Was: 145.9 MHz FM AFSK 2m receiver -- retargeted to all-UHF 2026-08-17.)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 27.94 29.4572 0)
		(size 134.62 27.515)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
			(color 0 0 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 255 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.397 1.397)
				(thickness 0.1746)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "d82f1b3e-9ad2-4ae8-b254-cc9e805ec44f")
	)
	(text_box "PSA4-5043+: broadband self-biased pHEMT LNA (0.05-4 GHz, internally 50-ohm matched). Vd applied at the RF_OUT pin through an RF choke; DC block C54 separates RF from bias. At 435 MHz: ~21 dB gain, ~0.7 dB NF, +20 dBm P1dB(out), 60 mA at Vd=+5V. Because the part is broadband, little/no band-specific input/output match is needed for 435.\n\nKEY UHF FIX: the RF_OUT bias choke (L14, currently 1 uH) must have SRF WELL above 435 MHz -- a 1 uH chip inductor likely self-resonates near/below our band and kills gain. Drop to a smaller high-SRF choke (~100-220 nH, SRF > 1 GHz), or a proper conical/RF choke. Grounding: tie pin 2 and the SOT-89 tab to a solid ground plane with multiple vias. Layout: keep input/output traces short, on opposite sides of the package."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 179.07 27.94 0)
		(size 78.74 22.86)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
			(color 0 0 0 1)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 150 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e8e2ac2f-d0f4-41e1-8a49-c559d861cb50")
	)
